        <bounds x="1430" y="560" width="160" height="55"/>
      </child>
      <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="pc5-note-0348" textAlignment="1">
        <bounds x="1250" y="20" width="340" height="500"/>
        <content>View name: Clinic Infrastructure View

Stakeholders: IT Manager, System Administrator

Concerns: What technology infrastructure is required to run the clinic's applications? Which applications are affected if a server or the external SMS/Email service fails?

Purpose: Show how each application component is deployed, which technology services it uses and how users connect.

Explanation: All four applications are deployed as artifacts on the Cloud Application Server, served by its Web Hosting Service. The server depends on the Data Storage Service of the Cloud Database Server, which is a single point of failure. The Notification Gateway depends on an external SMS/Email provider outside the clinic's control.</content>
      </child>
    </element>
